{"id":"mahabharata-10-003","work":"mahabharata","part":10,"partName":"सौप्तिकपर्व","partNameEn":"Sauptika Parva","unit":3,"title":"तृतीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 3 · Ashvatthaman resolves on a night attack","summary":{"en":"Ashvatthaman answers that he will not wait, since his father's death burns in him, and that he will kill the Panchalas in their sleep this night. He says he is ready to act, whatever the dharma of it.","kn":"ತಂದೆಯ ಸಾವು ತನ್ನನ್ನು ಸುಡುತ್ತಿರುವುದರಿಂದ ಕಾಯುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಈ ರಾತ್ರಿಯೇ ಪಾಂಚಾಲರನ್ನು ನಿದ್ರೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಕೊಲ್ಲುವೆನೆಂದು ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧರ್ಮ ಏನಾದರಾಗಲಿ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಸಿದ್ಧನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अश्वत्थामा उत्तर देता है कि पिता की मृत्यु उसे जला रही है, वह प्रतीक्षा नहीं करेगा और आज रात पाञ्चालों को सोते हुए मारेगा। वह कहता है कि धर्म जो भी हो, वह कार्य को तैयार है।","te":"తండ్రి మరణం తనను దహిస్తున్నందున వేచి ఉండనని, ఈ రాత్రే పాంచాలులను నిద్రలో చంపుతానని అశ్వత్థామ బదులిస్తాడు. ధర్మం ఏదైనా పని చేయడానికి సిద్ధమంటాడు.","ta":"தந்தையின் மரணம் தன்னை எரிப்பதால் காத்திருக்க மாட்டேன், இன்றிரவே பாஞ்சாலரை உறக்கத்தில் கொல்வேன் என்று அஸ்வத்தாமன் கூறுகிறான். தர்மம் எதுவாயினும் செயலுக்குத் தயார் என்கிறான்.","ml":"താൻ കാത്തിരിക്കില്ലെന്നും, പിതാവിന്റെ മരണം തന്നിൽ എരിയുന്നതിനാൽ ഇന്നുരാത്രി ഉറങ്ങുന്ന പാഞ്ചാലരെ കൊല്ലുമെന്നും അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് മറുപടി പറയുന്നു. അതിന്റെ ധർമ്മം എന്തുതന്നെയായാലും പ്രവർത്തിക്കാൻ താൻ തയ്യാറാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 10.3; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Fri Oct 30 2026","sections":[{"title":"सौप्तिकपर्व","titleEn":"Sauptika Parva (The night massacre)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कृपस्य वचनं श्रुत्वा धर्मार्थसहितं शुभम् ।\nअश्वत्थामा महाराज दुःखशोकसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard Kripa's good words, full of dharma and sense, Ashvatthaman, O great king, was consumed by grief and sorrow,"}},{"n":2,"text":"दह्यमानस्तु शोकेन प्रदीप्तेनाग्निना यथा ।\nक्रूरं मनस्ततः कृत्वा तावुभौ प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"burning with sorrow as with a blazing fire; hardening his heart, he answered the two of them."}},{"n":3,"text":"पुरुषे पुरुषे बुद्धिः सा सा भवति शोभना ।\nतुष्यन्ति च पृथक्सर्वे प्रज्ञया ते स्वया स्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"In each person a different judgment seems fine, and each is pleased with his own understanding."}},{"n":4,"text":"सर्वो हि मन्यते लोक आत्मानं बुद्धिमत्तरम् ।\nसर्वस्यात्मा बहुमतः सर्वात्मानं प्रशंसति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everyone in the world thinks himself the wiser; everyone esteems his own self and praises it."}},{"n":5,"text":"सर्वस्य हि स्वका प्रज्ञा साधुवादे प्रतिष्ठिता ।\nपरबुद्धिं च निन्दन्ति स्वां प्रशंसन्ति चासकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everyone's own understanding rests on his own approval, and they find fault with others' judgment while repeatedly praising their own."}},{"n":6,"text":"कारणान्तरयोगेन योगे येषां समा मतिः ।\nतेऽन्योन्येन च तुष्यन्ति बहु मन्यन्ति चासकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose minds agree on a matter because of some other shared reason are pleased with one another and often hold each other in high regard."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्यैव तु मनुष्यस्य सा सा बुद्धिस्तदा तदा ।\nकालयोगविपर्यासं प्राप्यान्योन्यं विपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"But in the very same man, as time and circumstances shift, one judgment after another comes and goes and contradicts the earlier."}},{"n":8,"text":"अचिन्त्यत्वाद्धि चित्तानां मनुष्याणां विशेषतः ।\nचित्तवैकल्यमासाद्य सा सा बुद्धिः प्रजायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because people's minds are beyond reckoning, especially in men, each new judgment arises from some disturbance of mind."}},{"n":9,"text":"यथा हि वैद्यः कुशलो ज्ञात्वा व्याधिं यथाविधि ।\nभेषजं कुरुते योगात्प्रशमार्थमिहाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a skilled physician, having diagnosed an illness correctly, prepares a medicine suited to curing it,"}},{"n":10,"text":"एवं कार्यस्य योगार्थं बुद्धिं कुर्वन्ति मानवाः ।\nप्रज्ञया हि स्वया युक्तास्तां च निन्दन्ति मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"so people form their judgment to carry out a task; they are guided by their own understanding, and yet people also blame it."}},{"n":11,"text":"अन्यया यौवने मर्त्यो बुद्ध्या भवति मोहितः ।\nमध्येऽन्यया जरायां तु सोऽन्यां रोचयते मतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A mortal is bewildered by one kind of reasoning in youth, by another in middle age, and in old age he prefers yet another view."}},{"n":12,"text":"व्यसनं वा पुनर्घोरं समृद्धिं वापि तादृशीम् ।\nअवाप्य पुरुषो भोज कुरुते बुद्धिवैकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Upon meeting a terrible disaster, or upon equal prosperity, O Bhoja, a man's judgment becomes altered."}},{"n":13,"text":"एकस्मिन्नेव पुरुषे सा सा बुद्धिस्तदा तदा ।\nभवत्यनित्यप्रज्ञत्वात्सा तस्यैव न रोचते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In one and the same man a different judgment arises at different times, because his understanding is unsteady, and that one does not please even him afterwards."}},{"n":14,"text":"निश्चित्य तु यथाप्रज्ञं यां मतिं साधु पश्यति ।\nतस्यां प्रकुरुते भावं सा तस्योद्योगकारिका ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having decided according to his understanding, whichever view a man sees as sound, he gives his heart to it, and it spurs him to action."}},{"n":15,"text":"सर्वो हि पुरुषो भोज साध्वेतदिति निश्चितः ।\nकर्तुमारभते प्रीतो मरणादिषु कर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Every man, O Bhoja, convinced that a thing is right, sets about doing it gladly, even in matters such as death."}},{"n":16,"text":"सर्वे हि युक्तिं विज्ञाय प्रज्ञां चापि स्वकां नराः ।\nचेष्टन्ते विविधाश्चेष्टा हितमित्येव जानते ॥","meaning":{"en":"All men, knowing the reasoning and their own understanding, undertake all sorts of actions, knowing it to be to their good."}},{"n":17,"text":"उपजाता व्यसनजा येयमद्य मतिर्मम ।\nयुवयोस्तां प्रवक्ष्यामि मम शोकविनाशिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The resolve that has arisen in me today was born of calamity; I will tell it to you both, for it is the destroyer of my grief."}},{"n":18,"text":"प्रजापतिः प्रजाः सृष्ट्वा कर्म तासु विधाय च ।\nवर्णे वर्णे समाधत्त एकैकं गुणवत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having created creatures and assigned them their duties, Prajapati set one special excellence in each class."}},{"n":19,"text":"ब्राह्मणे दममव्यग्रं क्षत्रिये तेज उत्तमम् ।\nदाक्ष्यं वैश्ये च शूद्रे च सर्ववर्णानुकूलताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the brahmin, steady self-control; in the kshatriya, supreme fiery energy; in the vaishya, skill; in the shudra, compliance with all the classes."}},{"n":20,"text":"अदान्तो ब्राह्मणोऽसाधुर्निस्तेजाः क्षत्रियोऽधमः ।\nअदक्षो निन्द्यते वैश्यः शूद्रश्च प्रतिकूलवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin without self-control is not good, a kshatriya without fiery energy is the lowest, a vaishya without skill is despised, and a shudra who is contrary is likewise."}},{"n":21,"text":"सोऽस्मि जातः कुले श्रेष्ठे ब्राह्मणानां सुपूजिते ।\nमन्दभाग्यतयास्म्येतं क्षत्रधर्ममनु ष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I was born in an excellent, well-honored family of brahmins, but through ill luck I have followed this warrior's duty."}},{"n":22,"text":"क्षत्रधर्मं विदित्वाहं यदि ब्राह्मण्यसंश्रितम् ।\nप्रकुर्यां सुमहत्कर्म न मे तत्साधु संमतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, knowing the warrior's duty, I were to do some very great deed while relying on the brahmin's status, it would not be approved by me."}},{"n":23,"text":"धारयित्वा धनुर्दिव्यं दिव्यान्यस्त्राणि चाहवे ।\nपितरं निहतं दृष्ट्वा किं नु वक्ष्यामि संसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having borne a divine bow and divine weapons in battle, how shall I speak in an assembly after seeing my father slain?"}},{"n":24,"text":"सोऽहमद्य यथाकामं क्षत्रधर्ममुपास्य तम् ।\nगन्तास्मि पदवीं राज्ञः पितुश्चापि महाद्युतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So today, following the warrior's duty as I wish, I will go to the path of the king and of my own greatly radiant father."}},{"n":25,"text":"अद्य स्वप्स्यन्ति पाञ्चाला विश्वस्ता जितकाशिनः ।\nविमुक्तयुग्यकवचा हर्षेण च समन्विताः ।\nवयं जिता मताश्चैषां श्रान्ता व्यायमनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tonight the Panchalas, believing themselves safe and victorious, will sleep, with yokes and armor laid aside and full of joy; they think us beaten and tired out by the exertion."}},{"n":26,"text":"तेषां निशि प्रसुप्तानां स्वस्थानां शिबिरे स्वके ।\nअवस्कन्दं करिष्यामि शिबिरस्याद्य दुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they sleep at night at ease in their own camp, I will make a hard attack on the camp."}},{"n":27,"text":"तानवस्कन्द्य शिबिरे प्रेतभूतान्विचेतसः ।\nसूदयिष्यामि विक्रम्य मघवानिव दानवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having raided the camp, I will boldly slay them, senseless and as if already dead, as Indra slew the danavas."}},{"n":28,"text":"अद्य तान्सहितान्सर्वान्धृष्टद्युम्नपुरोगमान् ।\nसूदयिष्यामि विक्रम्य कक्षं दीप्त इवानलः ।\nनिहत्य चैव पाञ्चालाञ्शान्तिं लब्धास्मि सत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I will boldly kill them all together, with Dhrishtadyumna at their head, as a blazing fire burns dry grass; and having killed the Panchalas, I shall find peace, best of men."}},{"n":29,"text":"पाञ्चालेषु चरिष्यामि सूदयन्नद्य संयुगे ।\nपिनाकपाणिः संक्रुद्धः स्वयं रुद्रः पशुष्विव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I will move among the Panchalas in battle, slaying them in fury, like Rudra himself, trident in hand, among beasts."}},{"n":30,"text":"अद्याहं सर्वपाञ्चालान्निहत्य च निकृत्य च ।\nअर्दयिष्यामि संक्रुद्धो रणे पाण्डुसुतांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, having slain and cut down all the Panchalas, I will in anger torment the sons of Pandu as well in the fight."}},{"n":31,"text":"अद्याहं सर्वपाञ्चालैः कृत्वा भूमिं शरीरिणीम् ।\nप्रहृत्यैकैकशस्तेभ्यो भविष्याम्यनृणः पितुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, making the earth a body of all the Panchalas, striking them one by one, I will be free of my debt to my father."}},{"n":32,"text":"दुर्योधनस्य कर्णस्य भीष्मसैन्धवयोरपि ।\nगमयिष्यामि पाञ्चालान्पदवीमद्य दुर्गमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Duryodhana, Karna, Bhishma and Saindhava I will send the Panchalas today along the road that is hard to travel."}},{"n":33,"text":"अद्य पाञ्चालराजस्य धृष्टद्युम्नस्य वै निशि ।\nविरात्रे प्रमथिष्यामि पशोरिव शिरो बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tonight, at midnight, I will forcibly crush the head of Dhrishtadyumna, king of the Panchalas, like that of a sacrificial beast."}},{"n":34,"text":"अद्य पाञ्चालपाण्डूनां शयितानात्मजान्निशि ।\nखड्गेन निशितेनाजौ प्रमथिष्यामि गौतम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tonight I will crush with a sharp sword the sleeping sons of the Pandavas and Panchalas, O son of Gotama's line."}},{"n":35,"text":"अद्य पाञ्चालसेनां तां निहत्य निशि सौप्तिके ।\nकृतकृत्यः सुखी चैव भविष्यामि महामते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having slain that Panchala army in the night's sleeping attack, I will be fulfilled and happy, O man of great mind."}}]}]}